                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "Honestly, SEASON: A Letter to the Future is one of those games that makes you want to slow down and enjoy the little things. There’s no need to rush or fight enemies. You just ride your bike, explore different places, take photos, record sounds, and talk to people along the way.\n\nWhat I love most is the atmosphere. The scenery is beautiful, the music is relaxing, and even the quiet moments feel special. Sometimes I found myself stopping just to look around and take in the view. The story also has a certain emotional feeling that stays with you after playing.\n\nOf course, the gameplay can feel a little slow, and if you’re looking for action or exciting challenges, this probably isn’t the game for you. But if you enjoy peaceful exploration and games that make you feel something, it’s definitely worth trying.\n\nSometimes you don’t need an exciting adventure. You just need a bike, a camera, and a little time to appreciate the world around you.",
